    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0844" n="832" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg832"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39)/33: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hamburg</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Keblinger</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-30T18:00:00+01:00">October 30, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 30—5:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Referring to my telegram No. 178 October 28, 2 p.m., steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Frode</hi> belonging to United Steamship Company at
                    Copenhagen with a cargo wood pulp bound for consignees unknown is now detained
                    by German authorities. Prize Commissioner requests evidence of American
                    destination of this cargo as in the case mentioned in my telegram 174. He is
                    also holding following vessels pending receipt of similar <pb facs="0845"
                        n="833" xml:id="pg833"/> evidence for their cargoes: <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hulda Thorden, Karin Thorden, Vilk, Petsamo, Koura, Greta</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Asturias</hi>.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d912-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Keblinger</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d912-f1" n="9" xml:id="d912-f1-content">
                <p>By November 2 the <hi rendition="#italic">Delaware, Aagot, Everoja, Eros,
                        Geisha</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic">Keila</hi> had been added to the
                    list of detained vessels; and by November 14 a total of 23 vessels and one cargo
                    destined for the United States was being detained.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
